---
system: sys-19-billing-subscription
flow_id: subscription-lifecycle
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/19-billing-subscription#subscription-lifecycle
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, BillingService, Stripe, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - GET /v1/billing/subscription
  - POST /v1/billing/subscription/cancel
  - POST /v1/billing/subscription/pause
  - POST /v1/billing/subscription/resume
externals: [Stripe]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - subscription_not_found
  - already_cancelled
  - cancellation_window_closed
  - stripe_unavailable
  - pause_already_used_this_cycle
  - parent_jwt_stale
idempotency: GET naturally idempotent; mutations dedup on X-Request-Id 24h
retry: caller-side exponential backoff on 5xx only
timeout: 3s p99 — Stripe-side mutations may be 1.5s p95
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant BillingService
    participant Stripe
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over ParentApp: parent in parent_settings views subscription tile

    ParentApp->>Gateway: GET /v1/billing/subscription + parent JWT Bearer
    Gateway->>BillingService: forward (JWT validated; read-only — 60s freshness not required)
    BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT subscriptions WHERE household_id=? (read-through)
    alt subscription_not_found
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: no rows
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 404 subscription_not_found
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 404
    else found
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: subscription row {state, current_period_end, pause_count_this_cycle, ...}
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {state, tier, current_period_end, cancel_at_period_end, pause_available}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end

    Note over ParentApp: parent selects mutation (cancel / pause / resume)
    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: all mutations require fresh parent JWT (ADR-0005 D6 — < 60s)

    alt cancel
        ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/billing/subscription/cancel {X-Request-Id} + parent JWT Bearer
        Gateway->>Gateway: auth-resolver — verify JWT freshness < 60s
        alt parent_jwt_stale
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 parent_jwt_stale — re-PIN required
        else already_cancelled
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT subscriptions WHERE household_id=?
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {state: 'cancelled'}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 409 already_cancelled
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409
        else cancellation_window_closed
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>BillingService: check cancellation window (e.g. within N days of start)
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 422 cancellation_window_closed
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 422
        else stripe_unavailable
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>Stripe: DELETE /v1/subscriptions/{stripe_subscription_id} {cancel_at_period_end: true}
            Stripe--xBillingService: 5xx / timeout
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 502 stripe_unavailable
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 502
        else cancel_success
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>Stripe: DELETE /v1/subscriptions/{stripe_subscription_id} {cancel_at_period_end: true}
            Stripe-->>BillingService: {status: 'active', cancel_at_period_end: true}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE subscriptions SET state='cancelled', canceled_at=now() WHERE household_id=?
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT audit_logs {action: 'subscription_cancel', actor_jti, household_id, ts}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {state: 'cancelled', active_until: current_period_end}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
            Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: subscription continues until current_period_end
        end
    else pause
        ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/billing/subscription/pause {X-Request-Id} + parent JWT Bearer
        Gateway->>Gateway: auth-resolver — verify JWT freshness < 60s
        alt parent_jwt_stale
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 parent_jwt_stale — re-PIN required
        else pause_already_used_this_cycle
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT subscriptions WHERE household_id=?
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {pause_count_this_cycle >= 1}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 422 pause_already_used_this_cycle
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 422
        else stripe_unavailable
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/subscriptions/{stripe_subscription_id} {pause_collection: {behavior: 'void'}}
            Stripe--xBillingService: 5xx / timeout
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 502 stripe_unavailable
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 502
        else pause_success
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/subscriptions/{stripe_subscription_id} {pause_collection: {behavior: 'void'}}
            Stripe-->>BillingService: {status: 'paused'}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE subscriptions SET state='paused', pause_count_this_cycle=pause_count_this_cycle+1
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT audit_logs {action: 'subscription_pause', actor_jti, household_id, ts}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {state: 'paused'}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
        end
    else resume
        ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/billing/subscription/resume {X-Request-Id} + parent JWT Bearer
        Gateway->>Gateway: auth-resolver — verify JWT freshness < 60s
        alt parent_jwt_stale
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 parent_jwt_stale — re-PIN required
        else stripe_unavailable
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/subscriptions/{stripe_subscription_id} {pause_collection: ''}
            Stripe--xBillingService: 5xx / timeout
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 502 stripe_unavailable
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 502
        else resume_success
            Gateway->>BillingService: forward
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/subscriptions/{stripe_subscription_id} {pause_collection: ''}
            Stripe-->>BillingService: {status: 'active'}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE subscriptions SET state='active'
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT audit_logs {action: 'subscription_resume', actor_jti, household_id, ts}
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {state: 'active'}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: timeout 3s p99 — Stripe mutations ~1.5s p95 — X-Request-Id 24h dedup — audit_logs row on every mutation
